{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463817792,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNTYwOTAwOTY=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453","origin":"github"},"title":"git annex direct mode vs. submodule -\u003e dead end? Doesn't look like it!","message":"Demo:\n\n```\n% mkdir testsuper\n% cd testsuper\n% git init\nInitialized empty Git repository in /media/mih/USB DISK/testsuper/.git/\n% git annex init\ninit  \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n\n  Detected a crippled filesystem.\n\n  Enabling direct mode.\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n% mkdir testsub\n% cd testsub\n% git init\nInitialized empty Git repository in /media/mih/USB DISK/testsuper/testsub/.git/\n% touch test\n% git add test\n% git commit -m commit\n[master (root-commit) 3fcd25e] commit\n 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 test\n% cd ..\n% git submodule add testsub testsub\nfatal: /usr/lib/git-core/git-submodule cannot be used without a working tree.\n% git annex proxy -- git submodule add testsub testsub\nfatal: /usr/lib/git-annex.linux/git-core/git-submodule cannot be used without a working tree.\n% git annex proxy -- git status\nOn branch annex/direct/master\n\nInitial commit\n\nUntracked files:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to include in what will be committed)\n\n    testsub/\n\nnothing added to commit but untracked files present (use \"git add\" to track)\n```\n\n`git annex proxy` generates a temporary working tree from commited and staged changes, hence it doesn't see the to-be-added submodule/directory. At this point, I don't see a workaround.\n\nThis issue should be limited to adding a fresh submodule to a dataset, and should not affect the consumption of subdatasets in installed datasets on crippled file systems.","files":null}]}